WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:05.250
You probably recognize Benjamin Joseph Manaly
Novak — known professionally as B.J.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.120
Novak — as Ryan from NBC's The Office.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:11.880
Or maybe you recognize him from one of his
many TV or movie appearances.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:15.940
Either way, though, you probably don't recognize
him from anything recent, because when it

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.470
comes to acting, he seems to have disappeared.

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:20.710
Here's a look at why Hollywood won't cast
B.J.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:22.259
Novak any more.

00:00:22.259 --> 00:00:24.239
He was never a leading man

00:00:24.239 --> 00:00:28.599
Before becoming an actor, Novak made a name
for himself as a stand-up comedian, performing

00:00:28.599 --> 00:00:32.259
on Late Night with Conan O'Brien and Comedy
Central's Premium Blend.

00:00:32.259 --> 00:00:37.580
In 2003, Variety named him one of its "Ten
Comics to Watch" thanks in part to his gig

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:41.360
as Ashton Kutcher's sidekick on MTV's celebrity
prank show Punk'd.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:44.800
And when he did break into acting, it was
in supporting roles.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.280
Besides The Office, Novak is probably best
known for small roles in Inglourious Basterds

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:54.430
and The Amazing Spider-Man 2, as well as cameos
in numerous TV shows.

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:59.079
But despite his success, Novak never became
a leading man - in part, because he was busy

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:01.280
with other interests off camera.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:04.799
"Well, back to the ol' XTC factory!"

00:01:04.799 --> 00:01:06.420
Major breakthrough

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:10.960
Shortly after getting his big break on Punk'd,
Novak caught the attention of The Office executive

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.219
producer Greg Daniels with a joke that would
change his life forever.

00:01:14.219 --> 00:01:16.240
"I learned nothing in college.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.100
It was really kind of my own fault.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:24.139
I had a double major: psychology and reverse
psychology."

00:01:24.139 --> 00:01:29.240
Daniels told The Boston Globe he knew "immediately"
after hearing it he wanted to work with Novak.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:34.219
Besides playing temp Ryan Howard, Novak became
more and more involved behind the scenes,

00:01:34.219 --> 00:01:37.170
ultimately writing and producing numerous
episodes.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:40.939
And when his long time friend and Office co-star
Mindy Kaling left to develop her own series,

00:01:40.939 --> 00:01:45.439
The Mindy Project, Novak took a job as one
of the show's producers, leaving little time

00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:47.289
for acting.

00:01:47.289 --> 00:01:48.289
Success as an author

00:01:48.289 --> 00:01:53.799
In 2013, Novak signed a seven figure book
deal with Knopf Doubleday Publishing Group

00:01:53.799 --> 00:01:57.639
around the same time his short story "The
Man Who Invented the Calendar" appeared in

00:01:57.639 --> 00:01:58.750
The New Yorker.

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:03.880
His first book, a collection of short stories
called One More Thing, was released in 2014

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:07.939
and received critical praise for its intelligent
satire and "tender heart."

00:02:07.939 --> 00:02:11.260
Novak hasn't just found success with an adult
audience, however.

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:15.090
He also penned the bestselling children's
book The Book With No Pictures — a strange

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:16.880
prospect for young readers.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:20.730
Novak told The Guardian, "I wanted to write
a book that would introduce the youngest of

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:26.910
kids to the idea that words can be their allies
— that the right words can be as fun, exciting,

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.930
and ridiculous as any pictures.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:30.950
Also, I can't draw."

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.770
He wants to direct

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:36.810
After playing a supporting role in Quentin
Tarantino's satirical war film Inglourious

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:41.270
Basterds, Novak realized that, in addition
to writing and producing, he's also interested

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:42.330
in directing.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:47.160
He told The Independent, "After I acted in
his film, I knew I wanted to direct.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:51.250
It feels like a natural extension — to take
something you've created all the way to the

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.530
finishing line.

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.780
That's why I visit schools now with my children's
book.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:58.260
I get real joy when I take my work directly
to the reader."

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:02.470
Thanks to The Office and The Mindy Project,
Novak had a chance to get his feet wet, directing

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:03.470
several episodes.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:06.090
"I feel like there's a voice in my head always.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:11.090
Telling me every idea is brilliant, and another
telling me every idea is the worst, and they

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.980
argue in my head."

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:13.980
He also made an app

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:21.980
In 2015, Novak developed an app called "The
List App," which allowed users to… well,

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.100
make a list.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:27.430
It sounds simple enough, but it proved to
be a hit, lasting for two years before Novak

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:30.400
shut it down in order to begin developing
a new app.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.020
So keep your eyes peeled!

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:33.900
A future in politics?

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:38.710
When he was young, Novak actually wanted to
be a real estate developer.

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:42.490
He told The Guardian, "I think I had some
vague awareness of Donald Trump.

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:47.790
Like, 'I want to put my name on buildings,
I want to be rich and important and a businessman!'"

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:51.600
So it's only fitting that he now wants to
follow Trump's lead by transitioning from

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.980
TV star to politician.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:58.350
But he doesn't want to be president - he wants
to become the mayor of Los Angeles.

00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:02.450
He told the Independent, "I'm not hugely political,
I just love my town…

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:05.319
I'm from Boston, but I live in the Hollywood
Hills.

00:04:05.319 --> 00:04:09.819
I've come to love the local side of L.A. much
more than the Hollywood side.

00:04:09.819 --> 00:04:12.319
I have dreams of running for mayor someday."

00:04:12.319 --> 00:04:16.570
Given how successful he has been with everything
else he's tried, we sure wouldn't put it past

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:17.570
him.

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:19.070
Good luck, Mayor Novak!

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.070
Thanks for watching!

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:22.600
